he user\'s previous get_metrics attempts had syntax errors. Maybe simplifying the query again. For example, checking the number of errors for each service. But since the previous attempt returned empty results, maybe the metrics aren\'t available or the query is incorrect. \n\nAlternatively, using get_operations on a service to see the specific operations and their metrics. For example, checking operations on \'frontend\' to see if certain endpoints are failing. \n\nBut given the tools available, the next logical step is to check the deployments and pods for any issues. So using exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd with "kubectl get deployments" in the \'astronomy-shop\' namespace. That would list all deployments and their statuses. If any deployment is in an error state, that\'s a starting point. \n\nSo the tool choice would be exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd with the command "kubectl get deployments -n astronomy-shop".\n</think>\n\nexec_read_only_kubectl_cmd  \nTo identify potential deployment issues (e.g., failed replicas, scaling problems), I\'ll check the deployments in the \'astronomy-shop\' namespace. This will reveal if any services are misconfigured or experiencing deployment failures.  \n\n<tool_call>\n{"name": "exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd", "arguments": {"command": "kubectl get deployments -n astronomy-shop"}}\n</tool_call>', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 841, 'prompt_tokens': 2834, 'total_tokens': 3675, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfe33-48a1-7f12-8742-bf07e3303f94-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 2834, 'output_tokens': 841, 'total_tokens': 3675}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, r