02b52491bf12d', 'operationName': 'oteldemo.CartService/GetCart', 'references': [{'refType': 'CHILD_OF', 'traceID': 'af36ed561102d37242e8434ba21e6d1c', 'spanID': '76f1d92b7675198f'}], 'startTime': 1773791214737000, 'duration': 3056, 'tags': [{'key': 'rpc.system', 'type': 'string', 'value': 'grpc'}, {'key': 'rpc.method', 'type", id='45298154-1413-4925-bc95-f4c7d3b5876c', tool_call_id='chatcmpl-tool-823950a03ac8f27b'), HumanMessage(content='You are now in the thinking stage. Choose a tool from the available tools and justify your choice.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='527c69d1-9fa5-44e9-8a2e-2ffa519b2ea9'), AIMessage(content='<think>\nOkay, let\'s see. The user is trying to diagnose an issue in the OpenTelemetry Demo Astronomy Shop application. They\'ve already checked the services, metrics, traces, and logs. The latest trace data shows a span with a feature flag key \'failedReadinessProbe\' and result \'off\'. Hmm, that might indicate a problem with the readiness probe of the \'flagd\' service. \n\nWait, the trace has a span where the feature flag \'failedReadinessProbe\' is being resolved. The value is \'off\', but maybe the readiness probe is failing, causing the service to not be ready. Let me check the deployment configuration for \'flagd\' to see if the readiness probe is misconfigured. \n\nI should use the `exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd` tool to get the deployment details for \'flagd\'. That way, I can check the readinessProbe settings. If the readiness probe is not set up correctly, like the path, port, or initial delay, it could cause the service to not be marked as ready, leading to issues in dependent services like \'cart\' that call \'flagd\'.\n\nSo the next step is to retrieve the deployment configuration for \'flagd\' to inspect its readiness probe settings. That should help identify if there\'s a misconfiguration causing the service to not be ready, which might be the root cause of the problem.\n</think>\n\nexec_read_only_kubectl_cmd  \nTo investigate potential readiness probe failures in the \'flagd\' service, I\'ll check its deployment configuration. The trace data showed a feature flag resolution for \'failedReadinessProbe\', suggesting a possible readiness probe issue. This step will confirm if the probe is misconfigured or failing.  \n\n<tool_call>\n{"name": "exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd", "arguments": {"command": "kubectl get deployment flagd -n astronomy-shop -o yaml"}}\n</tool_call>', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 381, 'prompt_tokens': 10878, 'total_tokens': 11259, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfe33-e855-7c40-9a98-2ba835723329-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 10878, 'output_tokens': 381, 'total_tokens': 11259}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='7348f638-a3ca-4910-a0e5-6bf2b130f70d'), AIMessage(content="<think>\nOkay, let's see. The user is trying to diagnose an issue in the OpenTelemetry Demo Astronomy Shop application. They've already checked the pods and found that all are running, but there's a trace indicating a possible problem with the 'flagd' service related to a readiness probe.\n\nThe user used the `get_traces` tool and found a span with the feature flag 'failedReadinessProbe'. That suggests that the readiness probe for the 'flagd' service might be failing. To confirm this, they need to check the deployment configuration of 'flagd' to see if the readiness probe is set up correctly.\n\nIn the previous step, the user called `kubectl get deployment flagd -n astronomy-shop -o yaml` to get the deployment details. The response from that command would include the readinessProbe configuration. If the readinessProbe is misconfigured, like having an incorrect endpoint, timeout, or failure threshold, that could cause the service to not be marked as ready, leading to issues in the application flow.\n\nLooking at the trace data, the span with 'failedReadinessProbe' might be related to the service not being ready when it's supposed to be, causing the feature flag resolution to fail. By examining the deployment YAML, the user can check the readinessProbe settings. If the probe is not working as expected, they can adjust the configuration to fix the issue.\n\nSo, the next step is to analyze the deployment YAML for the 'flagd' service. If the readinessProbe is misconfigured, that's the root cause. If everything looks good, maybe there's another issue, but the trace points towards the readiness probe being the problem. The user should check the probe's endpoint, initial delay, period, timeout, and failure thresholds. If the probe is correct, maybe there's a different issue, but based on the trace, the readiness probe seems like the likely culprit.\n</think>\n\n", additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl get deployment flagd -n astronomy-shop -o yaml"}', 'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-bec91f2930a4df9d', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 423, 'prompt_tokens': 11881, 'total_tokens': 12304, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfe33-fdd7-7b03-b472-d78e72b8ae23-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd', 'args': {'command': 'kubectl get deployment flagd -n astronomy-shop -o yaml'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-bec91f2930a4df9d', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 11881, 'output_tokens': 423, 'total_tokens': 12304}), ToolMessage(content='apiVersion: apps/v1\nkind: Deployment\nmetadata:\n  annotations:\n    deployment.kubernetes.io/revision: "1"\n    meta.helm.sh/release-name: astronomy-shop\n    meta.helm.sh/release-namespace: astronomy-shop\n  creationTimestamp: "2026-03-17T23:44:06Z"\n  generation: 1\n  labels:\n    app.kubernetes.io/component: flagd\n    app.kubernetes.io/managed-by: Helm\n    app.kubernetes.io/name: flagd\n    app.kubernetes.io/part-of: opentelemetry-demo\n    app.kubernetes.io/version: 2.2.0\n    helm.sh/chart: opentelemetry-demo-0.40.4\n    opentelemetry.io/name: flagd\n  name: flagd\n  namespace: astronomy-shop\n  resourceVersion: "348770"\n  uid: 3fb78447-47c8-4f36-851a-fd0377baaed8\nspec:\n  progressDeadlineSeconds: 600\n  replicas: 1\n  revisionHistoryLimit: 10\n  selector:\n    matchLabels:\n      opentelemetry.io/name: flagd\n  strategy:\n    rollingUpdate:\n      maxSurge: 25%\n      maxUnavailable: 25%\n    type: RollingUpdate\n  template:\n    metadata:\n      annotations:\n        resource.opentelemetry.io/service.namespace: otel-demo\n      creationTimestamp: null\n      labels:\n        app.kubernetes.io/component: flagd\n        app.kubernetes.io/name: flagd\n        app.kubernetes.io/version: 2.2.0\n        opentelemetry.io/name: flagd\n    spec:\n      containers:\n      - command:\n        - /flagd-build\n        - start\n        - --port\n        - "8013"\n        - --uri\n        - file:./etc/flagd/demo.flagd.json\n        env:\n        - name: OTEL_SERVICE_NAME\n          valueFrom:\n            fieldRef:\n              apiVersion: v1\n              fieldPath: metadata.labels[\'app.kubernetes.io/component\']\n        - name: OTEL_COLLECTOR_NAME\n          value: otel-collector\n        - name: OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_METRICS_TEMPORALITY_PREFERENCE\n          value: cumulative\n        - name: FLAGD_METRICS_EXPORTER\n          value: otel\n        - name: FLAGD_OTEL_COLLECTOR_URI\n          valu