in issue seems to be related to the \'flagd\' service, as indicated by the trace data mentioning a \'failedReadinessProbe\' feature flag. \n\nFirst, they checked the deployment YAML for \'flagd\' and didn\'t find any readiness or liveness probes. Then, they looked at the pod spec and saw that the containers are running, but there\'s no mention of probes there either. The traces show that there\'s a feature flag related to a failed readiness probe, which suggests that the service might not be ready when it\'s supposed to be, leading to potential issues with traffic routing or flag evaluations.\n\nSince the deployment and pod specs don\'t have probe configurations, the next step is to check if there\'s a ConfigMap or Secret that might contain the probe settings. Sometimes, configurations can be externalized into ConfigMaps or Secrets. The \'flagd\' pod has a volume mount for a ConfigMap named \'flagd-config\'. If the probe settings are stored there, checking the ConfigMap would be necessary.\n\nSo, the user should use the `exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd` tool to get the ConfigMap details. This will help determine if the readiness or liveness probes are configured there. If the ConfigMap doesn\'t have the probes, then the issue might be that the probes are missing entirely, leading to the service not being properly validated. Alternatively, there might be an environment variable or another configuration file that\'s not being checked yet. But given the current information, checking the ConfigMap is the logical next step.\n</think>\n\nexec_read_only_kubectl_cmd  \nThe `flagd` pod\'s spec and deployment do not explicitly define `readinessProbe` or `livenessProbe` configurations, yet traces reference a `failedReadinessProbe` feature flag. This suggests the service might be misconfigured or failing readiness checks. To confirm, I\'ll inspect the `flagd-config` ConfigMap (mounted in the pod) for probe-related settings.  \n\n<tool_call>\n{"name": "exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd", "arguments": {"command": "kubectl get configmap flagd-config -n astronomy-shop -o yaml"}}\n</tool_call>', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 478, 'prompt_tokens': 15585, 'total_tokens': 16063, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfe34-5fca-7393-a42f-5a773201c68f-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 15585, 'output_tokens': 478, 'total_tokens': 16063}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='a27cb4e4-d7d2-4f9b-b8dc-3cf73ecbbc1c'), AIMessage(content="<think>\nOkay, let's see. The user is trying to diagnose an issue in the OpenTelemetry Demo Astronomy Shop application. They've already checked the pods and deployments, looked at metrics, traces, and logs. The main issue seems to be related to the 'flagd' service, as indicated by the trace data mentioning a 'failedReadinessProbe' feature flag.\n\nFirst, the user checked the deployment YAML for 'flagd' and didn't find any readiness or liveness probes. Then they checked the pod spec, which also didn't have probe configurations. Now, they're looking into the ConfigMap named 'flagd-config' because the pod mounts it, and maybe the probe settings are there.\n\nThe next step is to retrieve the ConfigMap to see if there are any probe configurations defined in the flagd's configuration files. If the ConfigMap contains the 'demo.flagd.json' file, which is referenced in the pod's command, that file might have settings related to the feature flag or probes. By examining the ConfigMap, the user can check if there's a misconfiguration or if the readiness probe is set up incorrectly in the flagd service. This would help confirm if the issue is due to missing probes or incorrect settings in the configuration.\n</think>\n\n", additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl get configmap flagd-config -n astronomy-shop -o yaml"}', 'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-b38c8db0aa888022', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 295, 'prompt_tokens': 16612, 'total_tokens': 16907, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfe34-79d0-76f3-a844-633d8f4b9ccc-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd', 'args': {'command': 'kubectl get configmap flagd-config -n astronomy-shop -o yaml'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-b38c8db0aa888022', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 16612, 'output_tokens': 295, 'total_tokens': 16907}), ToolMessage(content='apiVersion: v1\ndata:\n  demo.flagd.json: |\n    {\n      "$schema": "https://flagd.dev/schema/v0/flags.json",\n      "flags": {\n        "llmInaccurateResponse": {\n          "defaultVariant": "off",\n          "description": "LLM returns an inaccurate product summary for product ID L9ECAV7KIM",\n          "state": "ENABLED",\n          "variants": {\n            "off": false,\n            "on": true\n          }\n        },\n        "llmRateLimitError": {\n          "defaultVariant": "off",\n          "description": "LLM intermittently returns a rate limit error",\n          "state": "ENABLED",\n          "variants": {\n            "off": false,\n            "on": true\n          }\n        },\n        "productCatalogFailure": {\n          "description": "Fail product catalog service on a specific product",\n          "state": "ENABLED",\n          "variants": {\n            "on": true,\n            "off": false\n      